  "summary": "Wilma Mankiller, born in Tahlequah, Oklahoma, in 1945, served as deputy chief of the Cherokee Nation from 1983 and became its principal chief in 1985, the first woman in that office. She received the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 1998 and died on 6 April 2010.",
